> **Rapid Revision Checklist — Must-Know Concepts for KTU Exam**

### Core Concepts
- ✅ **MapReduce** = Distributed parallel processing model with two user-defined functions: **Mapper** and **Reducer**.
- ✅ **Mapper** emits `<key, value>` pairs; **Reducer** aggregates values per key.
- ✅ **Shuffle & Sort** is framework-controlled (not user-defined) and groups all values for the same key.
- ✅ **Combiner** is an optional local reducer that reduces network traffic; requires associative & commutative operations.
- ✅ **Default Partitioner** is `HashPartitioner`: `index = hash(key) % numReducers`.

### Code Structure
- ✅ A MapReduce program has **3 classes**: Mapper, Reducer, and Driver.
- ✅ Mapper extends `Mapper<LongWritable, Text, Text, IntWritable>`.
- ✅ Reducer extends `Reducer<Text, IntWritable, Text, IntWritable>`.
- ✅ Driver configures the `Job` object and submits via `job.waitForCompletion(true)`.
- ✅ Use `context.write()` to emit key-value pairs.

### Keyword Filtering Specifics
- ✅ Use a `HashSet<String>` for **O(1) keyword lookup** performance.
- ✅ Always call `toLowerCase()` for **case-insensitive matching**.
- ✅ Use `replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z0-9]", "")` to **strip punctuation**.
- ✅ Initialize the keyword set in the **`setup()` method** (overridden from the parent class).

